#, no-c-format
msgid "Novell GroupWise Server"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:161
#, no-c-format
msgid "Addressbook on IMAP Server via Kmail"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:162
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This resource stores contacts as messages on an IMAP server. &kmail; is used "
"to access the IMAP server, therefore, if you use this type of resource, "
"&kmail; will open whenever you access the address book, if it (or &kontact;) "
"are not already running."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:171
#, no-c-format
msgid "LDAP"
msgstr "LDAP"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:172
#, no-c-format
msgid "All contacts will be stored on a LDAP server;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:176
#, no-c-format
msgid "Network"
msgstr "Ret"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:177
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"All contacts will be stored in one file, which can be located on a remote "
"server (for example, through &HTTP;, WebDAV, &FTP; or Fish)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:182
#, no-c-format
msgid "Addressbook on an Exchange Server (Experimental)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:187
#, no-c-format
msgid "OpenXchange Server"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:188
#, no-c-format
msgid "This resource stores contacts on an OpenExchange server."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:192
#, no-c-format
msgid "Suse Linux Openexchange Server"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:193
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This resource stores contacts on an OpenExchange or SUSE &Linux; "
"OpenExchange groupware server."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:197
#, no-c-format
msgid "eGroupware Server (via XML-RPC)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:203
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"After selecting the type of resource another dialog appears where you can "
"configure the resource-specific settings."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:204
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>File</guilabel> and <guilabel>Directory</guilabel> resource "
"supports different formats for storing the contacts:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:209 index.docbook:746
#, no-c-format
msgid "vCard"
msgstr "vCard"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:210
#, no-c-format
msgid "the contacts will be stored in the vCard format, as specified in RFC 2426;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:215
#, no-c-format
msgid "Binary"
msgstr "Binari"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:216
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"the contacts will be stored in a binary format &mdash; this increases "
"performance during loading and saving, but it is not portable like the vCard "
"format."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:222
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kaddressbook; needs a standard resource, where all contacts should be saved "
"if no other resource is specified; for this reason, after starting "
"&kaddressbook; the first time, there is already a resource available. If you "
"want to use another resource as the standard resource, use the "
"<guibutton>Use as Standard</guibutton> button to select it. You must have "
"both read and write access to the new standard resource, otherwise you won't "
"be able to select it."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:233
#, no-c-format
msgid "Managing Contacts"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:234
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To create or edit contacts, &kaddressbook; offers a dialog where you can "
"input all the data that can be stored in a vCard."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:239
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Contact Dialog"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:242
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>The Contact Dialog.</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:243
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>The Contact Dialog.</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:256
#, no-c-format
msgid "General Settings tab"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:257
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the <guilabel>General</guilabel> tab you can enter the basic information "
"about a contact, for example, addresses, phone numbers, and email addresses."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:261
#, no-c-format
msgid "Automatic Name Parsing"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:262
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kaddressbook; tries to provide an easy name input by automatic name "
"parsing; for this to work properly it is sometimes necessary to add custom "
"name prefixes, suffixes or inclusions in the <link linkend=\"preferences-"
"address-book-contact\">configure dialog</link>. However, no algorithm is "
"perfect, and rarely, a name may be parsed incorrectly; in this case, you can "
"disable the automatic name parsing in the name edit dialog, which is "
"available by clicking the <guibutton>Edit Name...</guibutton> button in the "
"contact dialog. If you wish to disable the name parsing for all new contacts "
"you can disable automatic name parsing globally in the <link linkend="
"\"preferences-address-book-general\">configure dialog</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:275
#, no-c-format
msgid "Formatted Name"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:276
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The formatted name of a contact is used by other programs to represent it. "
"&kaddressbook; offers three predefined types of formatted names:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:283
#, no-c-format
msgid "Custom"
msgstr "Personalizat"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:284
#, no-c-format
msgid "&lt;see below&gt;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:288
#, no-c-format
msgid "Simple Name"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:289
#, no-c-format
msgid "&lt;given name&gt; &lt;family name&gt;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:293
#, no-c-format
msgid "Full Name"
msgstr "Nom complet"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:294
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&lt;prefix&gt; &lt;given name&gt; &lt;additional name&gt; &lt;family "
"name&gt; &lt;suffix&gt;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:299
#, no-c-format
msgid "Reverse Name with Comma"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:300
#, no-c-format
msgid "&lt;family name&gt;, &lt;given name&gt;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:304
#, no-c-format
msgid "Reverse Name"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:305
#, no-c-format
msgid "&lt;family name&gt; &lt;given name&gt;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:309
#, no-c-format
msgid "Organisation"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:310
#, no-c-format
msgid "&lt;Organisation Name&gt;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:314
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If none of the above types fit your needs you can select the "
"<guilabel>Custom</guilabel> name type, where you can add your own formatted "
"name &mdash; this configuration can be done in the name edit dialog. To "
"specify a default formatted name type for new contacts, use the <link "
"linkend=\"preferences-address-book-contact\">configure dialog</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:324
#, no-c-format
msgid "Phone Numbers"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:325
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Here you can enter your contact's phone numbers. As well as land-lines and "
"mobile/cell number, Fax, ISDN and many other types are possible. The number "
"can contain almost any character, so it is possible to format the number in "
"any way you need, including adding letters."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:327
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If three numbers aren't enough, simply press the <guilabel>Add</guilabel> "
"button to get additional fields to enter a number."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:329
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If the type of the number is either a Phone, Mobile phone or Fax number you "
"can select a script to be executed when clicking on it. (under Configuration "
"→ General)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:335
#, no-c-format
msgid "Addresses"
msgstr "Adreças"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:336
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Here you can enter your contact's addresses. You can do so by pressing the "
"<guibutton>Edit Addresses...</guibutton> Button and simply enter the "
"<guilabel>Street</guilabel>, <guilabel>Post Office Box</guilabel>, "
"<guilabel>Locality</guilabel>, <guilabel>Postal Code</guilabel>, and "
"<guilabel>Country</guilabel>. After you do so you can look up the address on "
"the map by simply clicking on the address (you can change the map-service/"
"string used by &kaddressbook; in its settings."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:337
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can also create a label, which will be shown instead of the real address "
"(however, the map lookup, will use the real address)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:338
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can also have set different addresses (i.e. one for work and one for "
"home). It's also possible to set two different <guilabel>Home</guilabel> "
"addresses."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:342
#, no-c-format
msgid "Emails"
msgstr "Corrièl"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:343
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can enter email addresses for your contact here. You can set one address "
"as standard."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:344
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you set a photo for your contact on the <guilabel>Misc</guilabel> tab, "
"&kmail; will show it when viewing these addresses."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:345
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"These addresses will be used in &kmail; if you type the name of the person "
"in either the <guilabel>\"to\"</guilabel>, <guilabel>\"cc\"</guilabel> or "
"<guilabel>\"bcc\"</guilabel> field of a new message."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:349
#, no-c-format
msgid "Instant Messaging"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:350
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>IM Address</guilabel> text box holds the preferred Instant "
"Messaging Address for this contact. To add, view and edit additional IM "
"Addresses, click the <guibutton>Edit IM Addresses...</guibutton> button. The "
"<guilabel>Edit Instant Messaging Address</guilabel> dialog appears."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:354
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Edit IM Addresses Dialog"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:357
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>The Edit IM Addresses Dialog.</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:358
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>The Edit IM Addresses Dialog.</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:362
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A contact can have multiple instant messaging addresses associated with it. "
"Other applications, which are using the <application>Kimproxy</application> "
"system, such as &kopete; or &konversation; can interact using this "
"information. So in example you can associate a contact in IRC with a contact "
"in your address book. This cannot be done automatically, you have to make "
"this association manually in the specific program."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:364
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you are not interest in whether they are picked up in another "
"application, and just want to store the instant messaging addresses with the "
"contact, then it's fine to add and edit them here. Otherwise it's "
"recommended that you let the applications do the changes and not yourself, "
"to not interfere with them."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:366
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For more information on adding new Instant Messaging Addresses, see <ulink "
"url=\"help:/kopete/getting-started.html#creating-accounts\">&kopete;'s "
"handbook</ulink> and <ulink url=\"help:/konversation/linkaddressbook.html"
"\">&konversation;'s handbook</ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:374
#, no-c-format
msgid "Categories"
msgstr "Categorias"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:375
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Categories help you to sort and group your contacts. You can simply add a "
"contact to one or more groups by pressing the <guibutton>Select Categories..."
"</guibutton> button."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:376
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To add your own category or remove an unused category you can click on "
"<guibutton>Edit Categories...</guibutton>. Here you can edit, add and remove "
"categories. Please notice that it is automatically started in Edit mode."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:380
#, no-c-format
msgid "Public, Private and Confidental"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:381
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The three modes Public, Private and Confidental are part of the vCard "
"standart and implemented as such. These allow you another way to group your "
"contacts."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:386
#, no-c-format
msgid "Details tab"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:387
#, no-c-format
msgid "This is the place where you can store additional details on your contacts."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:388
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The fields are mostly self-explanatory. You will notice that the "
"<guilabel>Anniversary</guilabel> and <guilabel>Birthday</guilabel> dates are "
"listed in the <guilabel>Special Dates</guilabel> list in the &kontact; "
"summary."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:392
#, no-c-format
msgid "Crypto Settings tab"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:393
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In this tab, you can define preferences with regards to cryptography for a "
"contact. At the time of this writing, only &kmail; and &kontact; will make "
"use of these preferences when composing messages. This mechanism replaces "
"the barely editable per-recipient crypto preferences of earlier &kmail; "
"releases."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:404
#, no-c-format
msgid "Allowed Protocols"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:407
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Here, you can restrict the cryptographic message formats that can be used "
"for this contact. See the section on <ulink url=\"/kmail/the-composer-window."
"html#cryptographic-message-formats\">Cryptographic Message Formats</ulink> "
"in <ulink url=\"/kmail/\">&kmail;'s handbook</ulink> for a discussion of the "
"different available formats."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:420
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Preferred OpenPGP encryption key</guilabel>, <guilabel>Preferred "
"&smime; encryption certificate</guilabel>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:425
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Here, you can assign a preferred OpenPGP key and/or &smime; certificate to "
"be used when encrypting to this contact. Otherwise, the local keyring and "
"local certificate box are searched for matching keys and certificates."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:436
#, no-c-format
msgid "Message Preference"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:439
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Here, you can select from a set of directives for user interaction both when "
"signing and when encrypting."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:446
#, no-c-format
msgid "&lt;none&gt;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:449
#, no-c-format
msgid "No preference, use whatever mode &kmail; defaults to."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:456
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Never Sign</guilabel>, <guilabel>Never Encrypt</guilabel>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:460
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Never sign (encrypt) messages to this contact. Don't ask for confirmation "
"(except in the case of conflicts with preferences of other contacts)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:469
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Always Sign</guilabel>, <guilabel>Always Encrypt</guilabel>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:474
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Always sign (encrypt) messages to the contact. Don't ask for confirmation "
"(except in the case of conflicts with preferences of other contacts)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:483
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Always Sign If Possible</guilabel>, <guilabel>Always Encrypt If "
"Possible</guilabel>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:488
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Always sign (encrypt) messages to this contact when it would be possible to "
"do so. Don't ask if it isn't possible. Situations in which signing might not "
"be possible include other recipients having signing preferences of \"Never"
"\". Situations in which encryption might not be possible include missing "
"keys/certificates for this or other recievers."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:502
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Ask</guilabel>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:505
#, no-c-format
msgid "Always ask whether to sign (encrypt)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:516
#, no-c-format
msgid "Misc tab"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:517
#, no-c-format
msgid "This describes the <guilabel>Misc</guilabel> settings tab"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:520
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>Geo Data</title>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:521
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Here you can enter the contact's geographical location, with "
"<guilabel>Latitude</guilabel> and <guilabel>Longitude</guilabel>. To \"enable"
"\" them simply click on the check box <guilabel>use geo data</guilabel>. "
"After that you can either enter the coordinates by hand or click on "
"<guilabel>Edit Geo Data...</guilabel> to select them on a world map."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:524
#, no-c-format
msgid "Sound"
msgstr "Son"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:525
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can store a spoken version of the name here. It is helpful for foreign "
"names."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:526
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"However this is part of the vCard 2.1 standard and only supports the three "
"formats: WAVE, PCM, AIFF."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:527
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select <guibutton>Store as URL</guibutton> if the sound lies on a remote "
"machine."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:530
#, no-c-format
msgid "Photo and Logo"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:531
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"By clicking on the buddy icon you can select and scale a picture of your "
"contact."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:532
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The Photo will be shown in the contact preview and in the Icon view mode. "
"However the Logo picture will only be shown in Icon view and only if there's "
"no photo available."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:533
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To reset a photo or logo simply right click on it and select "
"<guilabel>Reset</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:536
#, no-c-format
msgid "Location of Free/Busy informations"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:537
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Here you can select a path to a contact's Free/Busy information, which are "
"used when you add him to an event in &korganizer; or &kontact;'s calendar "
"view."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:543
#, no-c-format
msgid "Custom Fields Tab"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:544
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the <guilabel>Custom Fields</guilabel> Tab you can add your own fields, "
"either for just the current contact or for all. The following types of "
"fields are possible:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:548
#, no-c-format
msgid "Text"
msgstr "Tèxt"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:551
#, no-c-format
msgid "Here you can enter every alphanumeric symbol"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:557
#, no-c-format
msgid "Numeric Value"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:560
#, no-c-format
msgid "You can only enter numbers here."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:566
#, no-c-format
msgid "Boolean"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:569
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Boolean is only yes or no(true or false, or however you want to call it). In "
"KAddressbook it's a simply check box you can check or uncheck it."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:575
#, no-c-format
msgid "Date"
msgstr "Data"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:578
#, no-c-format
msgid "Here you can enter a date."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:584
#, no-c-format
msgid "Time"
msgstr "Ora"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:587
#, no-c-format
msgid "Here you can enter a time value."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:593
#, no-c-format
msgid "Date &amp; Time"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:596
#, no-c-format
msgid "Here you can enter both, a date and a time."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:608
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using Views"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:609
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In this version, &kaddressbook; offers different views, which can represent "
"the contacts in three different ways:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:616
#, no-c-format
msgid "Table View"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:617
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"All contacts are listed in a table; they can be sorted by clicking at the "
"column header of the table. The columns of the table depend on the fields "
"which were selected in the view configuration dialog."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:624
#, no-c-format
msgid "Icon View"
msgstr "Visualizacion en icònas"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:625
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The contacts are listed as icons in a view. If the contact contains a photo "
"or logo, then it is used in the view; otherwise, an default icon is used."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:631
#, no-c-format
msgid "Card View"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:632
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"All contacts are presented in form of cards. The titles of these cards are "
"the formatted names; the body of each card depends on what fields were "
"selected in the view configuration dialog."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:639
#, no-c-format
msgid "The View Configuration Dialog"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:642
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>The View Configuration Dialog.</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:643
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>The View Configuration Dialog.</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:647
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Selected Fields</guilabel> page offers you the possibility of "
"selecting which of the stored details of a contact should be shown in the "
"view. In the <guilabel>Default Filter</guilabel> page you can setup what "
"<link linkend=\"using-filters\">filter</link> should be used by the view."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:654
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using Filters"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:655
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can setup filters in &kaddressbook; which depend on the categories a "
"contact belongs to. For example, you can create a filter that matches all "
"contacts which belong to the categories 'Family' and 'Friends'; you can also "
"create a filter that matches all contacts which do not these categories. To "
"manage filters, use the filter configuration dialog:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:664
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Filter Configuration Dialog"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:667
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>The Filter Configuration Dialog.</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:668
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>The Filter Configuration Dialog.</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:672
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Filters can be used in views to reduce the number of contacts shown. In the "
"<link linkend=\"using-filters\">view configuration dialog</link> you can "
"specify what filter should be used by a view by default."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:680
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using Extensions"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:681
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Extensions are implemented as plugins in &kaddressbook;, so 3rd-party "
"developers can provide more of them. At the moment we already have three "
"extensions:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:689
#, no-c-format
msgid "None"
msgstr "Pas cap"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:690
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This selection shows no extension. This is a good default selection, if "
"you're not using any of the other extensions because it saves space."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:694
#, no-c-format
msgid "Contact Editor"
msgstr "Editor de contactes"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:695
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Similar to the the contact editing dialog, but designed to allow contacts to "
"be edited quickly."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:700
#, no-c-format
msgid "Address Books"
msgstr "Quasernets d'adreças"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:701
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This extension shows you a list of available address book resources. You can "
"check/uncheck them to show/hide the entries of a specific address book."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:702
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"It is also possible to <guilabel>Add</guilabel>, <guilabel>Edit</guilabel> "
"or <guilabel>Remove</guilabel> an resource, for more information about this "
"see <link linkend=\"configure-resources\">how to configure resources</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:706
#, no-c-format
msgid "Distribution List Manager"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:707
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This extension provides easy management of email distribution lists: just "
"create a new list and select a contact in the view; then, after clicking "
"<guibutton>Add contact</guibutton>, the selected contact is part of the "
"distribution list. A simpler way is to drag a contact from the view and drop "
"it over the distribution list manager. See <link linkend=\"settings-menu\"> "
"Settings Menu</link> about how to add an extension."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:717
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>The main window with distribution list extension.</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:720
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>The main window with distribution list extension.</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:721
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>The main window with distribution list extension.</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:727
#, no-c-format
msgid "Import and Export"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:728
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"With the new import/export framework &kaddressbook; offers a dialog where "
"you can select which contacts are to be exported."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:732
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>The export selection dialog.</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:735
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>The export selection dialog.</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:736
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>The export selection dialog.</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:741
#, no-c-format
msgid "Import"
msgstr "Importar"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:742
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kaddressbook; is able to import the following formats:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:747
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"With this entry you can import your contacts from the vCard format "
"(<acronym>RFC</acronym> 2426)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:751
#, no-c-format
msgid "MS Exchange Personal Address Book (.PAB)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:752
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"With this entry you can import your contacts from your Address book on a MS "
"Exchange personal address book, which is used by MS Outlook and MS Outlook "
"Express to store their contact data."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:757
#, no-c-format
msgid "Eudora Addressbook"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:758
#, no-c-format
msgid "With this plugin you can import your contacts from the Eudora mail client."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:764 index.docbook:802
#, no-c-format
msgid "CSV List"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:765
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"CSV (comma separated value) is a format that is used by many (address book) "
"applications."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:770
#, no-c-format
msgid "Opera Addressbook"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:771
#, no-c-format
msgid "With this entry you can import your contacts from the Opera web browser."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:775
#, no-c-format
msgid "KDE 2 Addressbook"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:776
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"With this entry you can import your old contacts from a &kde; 2.x "
"installation."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:780 index.docbook:808
#, no-c-format
msgid "LDIF Addressbook"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:781 index.docbook:809
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"LDIF is a plain-text representation of LDAP data, used by &Netscape; and "
"Mozilla to store their address book data."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:785 index.docbook:813
#, no-c-format
msgid "GMX Address Book"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:786 index.docbook:814 index.docbook:824
#, no-c-format
msgid "To be written."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:792
#, no-c-format
msgid "Export"
msgstr "Exportar"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:793
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kaddressbook; is able to export into the following formats:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:797
#, no-c-format
msgid "vCard 2.1 &#038; 3.0"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:798
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"With this entry you can import your contacts from the vCard format "
"(<acronym>RFC</acronym> 2426). You can either export it into the 2.1 or in "
"the 3.0 compatibel version of the vCard standard."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:803
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"CSV (comma separated value) is a format that is used by many (address book) "
"applications, it stores the contact informations in a plaintext field "
"seperated by commas. This makes CSV very flexible and good for interaction "
"with scripts."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:818
#, no-c-format
msgid "Bookmarks Menu"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:819
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This exports the stored URLs of your contacts into the &konqueror; bookmarks "
"system."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:823
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Geo Data</guilabel>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:833
#, no-c-format
msgid "LDAP queries"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:834
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Address information from LDAP servers can be imported into &kaddressbook;'s "
"local address book by using the LDAP search dialog."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:838
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To configure (a number of) LDAP servers, use the <link linkend=\"preferences-"
"ldap-lookup\">configuration dialog.</link>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:842
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"On the main toolbar in &kaddressbook; a button with a picture of a "
"magnifying glass over a book is available: use this button to open the LDAP "
"search dialog. The dialog itself is pretty straight forward; just type in "
"parts of a name, email address or phone number and press the "
"<guibutton>Search</guibutton> button."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:849
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When the results display in the listbox it is possible to select one or more "
"address(es); you can then use the <guibutton>Add Selected</guibutton> to "
"import the selected address(es) to the local address book, or click the "
"<guibutton>Send email to Contact</guibutton> to invoke a mail program to "
"write an email to the selected recipients."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:855
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guibutton>Recursive search</guibutton> check box is enabled by default; "
"this will make the LDAP query consider all objects below the base DN of each "
"server. If you only want to consider objects one level below the base "
"uncheck this check box; if in doubt, leave it checked."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:865
#, no-c-format
msgid "Preferences"
msgstr "Preferéncias"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:867
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can modify many aspects of &kaddressbook;'s behavior in the preferences "
"dialog; the dialog can be opened via <menuchoice><guimenu>Settings</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem>Configure KAddressBook...</guimenuitem></menuchoice> or "
"using the toolbar icon."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:873
#, no-c-format
msgid "Configuring &kaddressbook;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:876
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>The preferences dialog.</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:877
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>The preferences dialog.</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:882
#, no-c-format
msgid "The <guilabel>General</guilabel> Page"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:885
#, no-c-format
msgid "The <guilabel>General</guilabel> Tab"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:889
#, no-c-format
msgid "Honor &kde; single click"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:890
#, no-c-format
msgid "If checked, &kaddressbook; pays attention to the &kde; single-click option."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:895
#, no-c-format
msgid "Automatic Name Parsing for new addresses"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:896
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If checked, the <link linkend=\"managing-contacts-automatic-nameparsing"
"\">automatic name parsing</link> feature is used for new addresses."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:901
#, no-c-format
msgid "Limit unfiltered display to 100 contacts"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:902
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If checked, &kaddressbook; will only display 100 contacts in the contact "
"list, when no filter is applied."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:906
#, no-c-format
msgid "Addressee editor type"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:907
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can either select the \"<guilabel>Simple Editor</guilabel>\" or the "
"\"<guilabel>Full Editor</guilabel>\"."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:908
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The Simple editor mode only lets you enter the name (which will be "
"automaticly parsed, if enabled) and an email address."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:912
#, no-c-format
msgid "Script Hooks"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:913
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Here you can specify commands which are to be executed whenever you click at "
"a (mobile) phone number or fax number or SMS link in the details page."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:921
#, no-c-format
msgid "The <guilabel>Contact</guilabel> Tab"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:922
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kaddressbook; can automatically parse a name into its parts; to make sure "
"this works in many cases you can add, here, additional name parts, like "
"prefixes, suffixes and inclusions."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:929
#, no-c-format
msgid "Prefixes"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:930
#, no-c-format
msgid "Here you can manage name prefixes, like 'Prof.' or 'Dr.'."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:935
#, no-c-format
msgid "Inclusions"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:936
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Here you can manage name inclusions, like 'van' or 'von', which are often "
"part of Dutch or German names."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:941
#, no-c-format
msgid "Suffixes"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:942
#, no-c-format
msgid "Here you can manage name suffixes like 'Sr.' or 'Jr.'."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:947
#, no-c-format
msgid "Default Formatted Name"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:948
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Here you can select the default type of formatted names to be used for new "
"contacts."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:956
#, no-c-format
msgid "The <guilabel>LDAP Lookup</guilabel> Page"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:958
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"On this page you can configure the LDAP servers that should be used for "
"<link linkend=\"ldap-queries\">ldap queries</link> in &kaddressbook;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:961
#, no-c-format
msgid "Use <guibutton>Add Host...</guibutton> to add and setup a new server."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:963
#, no-c-format
msgid "Configuring LDAP Lookup"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:966
#, no-c-format
msgid "Example of LDAP Lookup configuration."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:967
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Add Host dialog - Example of LDAP Lookup configuration."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:970
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Please notice that some of the fields might be disabled, depending on your "
"selections."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:971
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can include and exclude servers from the search by selecting or "
"deselecting their check boxes. In the server list. Press <guibutton>OK</"
"guibutton> to close the dialog."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:974
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You may configure the search order by moving the servers up or down in the "
"list. This can be done using the arrows on the right side of the dialog."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:977
#, no-c-format
msgid "The <guilabel>Custom Pages</guilabel> Page"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:978
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This section allows you to add your own &GUI; elements ('Widgets') to store "
"your own values into &kaddressbook;. Proceed as described below:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: member
#: index.docbook:980
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"1. Click on <guibutton>Edit with QT Designer</guibutton>.(note: &Qt; "
"Designer has to be installed, otherwise the button is disabled)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: member
#: index.docbook:983
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"2. In the dialog, select <guilabel>Widget</guilabel>, then click "
"<guibutton>OK</guibutton>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: member
#: index.docbook:986
#, no-c-format
msgid "3. Add your widgets to the form."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: member
#: index.docbook:990
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"4. Save the file in the folder proposed by <application>&Qt; Designer</"
"application>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: member
#: index.docbook:994
#, no-c-format
msgid "5. Close <application>&Qt; Designer</application>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:998
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In case you already have a designer file (*.ui) located somewhere on your "
"hard disk, simply choose <guibutton>Import Page...</guibutton>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:999
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"IMPORTANT: The name of each input widget you place within the form must "
"start with 'X_'; so if you want the widget to correspond to your custom "
"entry 'X-Foo', set the widget's name property to 'X_Foo'."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1000
#, no-c-format
